  "_description": "Variant registry for familiar.realm.watch slot picker. Ops-owned. Edit alongside the systemd units in ops/systemd/units/ and the allow-list in allowed-units.txt. Copy to /var/lib/familiar/registry.json on the familiar host. REFRESHED 2026-08-09 for the B60 era: one CUDA GPU remains (P102-100, device 0, UUID-pinned in units); the Arc Pro B60 runs qwen3-coder.service (Vulkan, :8091) OUTSIDE the slot system. Removed extractor-phi4-mini-gpu1 (9.5GB + resident embed left a 256MiB nondeterministic margin - admission must hard-fail, not flap) and chat-ollama-qwen-3b (registry claimed ollama/qwen2.5-3b/2.3GB but the unit actually runs phi-4 14B via llama-server override at ~9.4GB - same marginal-fit class; unit remains on disk for manual use). Former GPU1 variants are re-keyed to device 0. vram_mb column re-baselined against embed (~400MiB) being permanently resident on the P102.",
